Hi there!

I've been reading RGRN for a long time now, but never felt the urge to
actually post something. However, I could use some opinions on my
current game, and it seems there are lots of nice people here :-),
so... here we go.


--- skip the following passage if you don't care about my recent
nethacking history ---

First off, I haven't had an ascension yet :( .. despite the fact that
I've been playing the game on and off for years. After playing valks
for a long, long, long time, losing virtually hundreds of them, I
finally decided to try something slightly different. You know, I had
lost three promising valks in a row. Finaya died in Gehennom to a
*trice because I was tired at that time and somehow didn't get the
message when I saw the words "Your limbs are stiffening" on my screen.
Tharonia also perished down there because of.. um, let's just call it
pure stupidity. And then I lost my last one on the plane of air - she
died six times to a seemingly endless horde of horned devils, for some
reason the whole level was filled with them. When she ran out of =oLS
(and I ran out of ideas how to deal with those guys), Veryssa finally
bit the dust as well. I was so close, damnit!

Being somewhat fed up with my lawful human female hammer-throwing
girls, I opted for a change, albeit a small one, because I just didn't
feel patient enough for one of the caster classes.

So, Gruumsh the chaotic orcish barbarian was born. After YASD'ing some
of his early incarnations, one of them finally made it quite far and
even went home to kick Thoth Amon's arse, when some freakin' ogre on
Qlvl 3 decided to play around with a !oParalysis. It crashed on
Gruumsh's head and he made a nice meal for a group of rock trolls.

His brother Grawl (I usually change my character's names after losing a
promising incarnation of them) then took up the quest to retrieve the
amulet, and he's doing well so far.

--- end of story ---



So, mighty Grawl is currently sitting at his altar stash on Dlvl15.
He'd went all the way down to Gehennom already, cleared out Asmodeus'
lair and then came back up to stash the phat lewt. After using Cleaver
for an incredibly long time (Set was stingy with artifacts), he finally
got Frostbrand (nicknamed it "potion-killer" - jeez, that potion
freezing effect is annoying), enchanted it to +7 and will probably use
it for the rest of the game.

Now, I'm wondering what I should use as a second weapon. All my valks
had been using Mojo (with GoP) and a mirror shield, so I'd really like
to try two-weapon combat for a change. My barb is wearing SDSM and
therefore doesn't need the shield anyway. I read lots of YAAP postings
here and I know the usual candidates for off-hand weapons, but it
doesn't seem to be all that obvious for a barbarian.

My thoughts so far:

* silver saber
Certainly useful in Gehennom against all the silver-hating stuff.
However, barbarians can't enhance sabers beyond basic skill.

* crysknife
I read stories about crysknives being awesome weapons. Barbs are
restricted in knives though, so they don't seem to be the best choice
here.

* ordinary axe or hammer
Nothing special, but I can train their corresponding skills to expert
level!

I'm not even sure if #twoweapon'ing with a barbarian is such a good
idea after all, as they can only enhance it to basic. I'm thinking of
using an elven shield for an additional -9 AC if you're going to tell
me that dual-wielding barbarians suck.

Any opinions are appreciated! :-)


